diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 503522b..82e6d7d 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@ Open the local URL printed by Vite. Run `npm run build` for a production build o
 
 - `src/lessons.js` defines the labels, part explanations and animation steps.
 - `src/narration-clips.js` maps narration and transcripts to lesson and part IDs. `src/narration.js` owns the single audio player; `src/narration-ui.js` renders its controls and transcript.
-- `src/models/` defines the four editable, procedural 3D models and their animations.
+- `src/models/` defines the 3D lessons and their animations. The Human Body lesson loads an adapted BodyParts3D cutaway. See [3D model credits](public/human-body-credits.txt) for sources and license details.
 - `src/viewer.js` handles the 3D camera, model selection and controls. The renderer uses WebGL 2 when available and falls back to Canvas 2D.
 - `src/style.css` defines the space-inspired UI, responsive layout and visual controls.
 - `public/eis-logo.png` is the supplied EIS mark.
diff --git a/public/human-body-credits.txt b/public/human-body-credits.txt
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c7f0838
--- /dev/null
+++ b/public/human-body-credits.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+Unfold | Human Body model credits
+
+BodyParts3D, © The Database Center for Life Science licensed under
+CC Attribution 4.0 International.
+Dataset and terms: https://dbarchive.biosciencedbc.jp/en/bodyparts3d/lic.html
+License: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
+Source archive: https://dbarchive.biosciencedbc.jp/en/bodyparts3d/download.html
+Source data: version 4.0, IS-A and PART-OF reduced polygon archives.
+Lung parenchyma: BodyParts3D 4.3, elements FJ6595–FJ6612,
+retrieved through Oliver Case’s verified BodyParts3D mesh collection:
+https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22727173
+
+Unfold adapts these meshes by selecting structures, simplifying geometry,
+joining the lung segments by lobe, aligning and scaling the models, and
+applying educational cutaways and colours. Breathing, heartbeat and blood
+flow markers are illustrative animations.
+
+The adapted model is also offered under the legacy archive’s
+CC Attribution-ShareAlike 2.1 Japan terms.
+https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.1/jp/
